1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:06,520
Water pollution is a serious problem around the world, and it is difficult to deal with.
水污染在世界各地都是一个严重的问题，而且很难应对。

2
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:10,840
Traditional water sensors can only work in fixed places.
传统的水质传感器只能在固定的地点工作。

3
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:17,020
As a result, they cannot cover large water bodies like rivers, lakes or oceans.
因此，它们无法覆盖河流、湖泊或海洋这样的大片水域。

4
00:00:17,820 --> 00:00:22,880
To solve this problem, scientists created a bionic tool—a robotic fish.
为了解决这个问题，科学家造出了一种仿生工具——机器鱼。

5
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:26,540
The robotic fish is a great example of bionics.
机器鱼是仿生学的一个绝佳例子。

6
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:30,500
It shows how scientists copy nature to solve problems.
它展示了科学家如何模仿大自然来解决问题。

7
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,670
In fact, the idea of copying nature is not new.
事实上，模仿大自然这一想法并不新鲜。

8
00:00:35,470 --> 00:00:39,470
The Wright brothers created their first plane by studying the flight of birds.
莱特兄弟通过研究鸟类的飞行，造出了自己的第一架飞机。

9
00:00:40,270 --> 00:00:45,010
Modern scientists created robotic fish by studying the swimming skills of trout.
现代科学家通过研究鳟鱼的游泳本领，造出了机器鱼。

10
00:00:45,810 --> 00:00:49,420
Trout are good at moving fast in water with very little energy.
鳟鱼擅长用很少的能量在水中快速游动。

11
00:00:50,220 --> 00:00:55,940
By “learning” the way trout move, robotic fish can work for ten hours after they are fully charged.
通过“学习”鳟鱼的游动方式，机器鱼充满电后可以工作十个小时。

12
00:00:56,740 --> 00:01:04,020
According to scientists, the robotic fish has a special soft tail, so it can swim quietly and smoothly under water.
据科学家介绍，机器鱼有一条特殊的软尾巴，所以能在水下安静、平稳地游动。

13
00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:08,880
It will not scare water animals or harm the underwater environment.
它不会惊扰水生动物，也不会损害水下环境。

14
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:15,160
Because of the small sensors inside its “body”, it can “taste” water to find harmful things.
由于“身体”里装有小型传感器，它能“品尝”水，从中找出有害物质。

15
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:22,420
Once the robotic fish finds water pollution, it will send a warning message to a central computer at once.
机器鱼一旦发现水污染，就会立即向中央计算机发送警报信息。

16
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:29,710
The robotic fish can even “eat” small pieces of plastic in water bodies and repair itself when it gets broken.
机器鱼甚至能“吃”掉水域中的小块塑料，还能在损坏时自我修复。

17
00:01:30,510 --> 00:01:36,080
Now more and more robotic fish are being used in rivers, lakes and oceans all over the world.
如今，世界各地的河流、湖泊和海洋中，投入使用的机器鱼越来越多。

18
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:40,100
They work together as a team to reduce water pollution.
它们组成一个团队协同工作，以减少水污染。

19
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:48,290
By copying nature, scientists have offered lots of possibilities for protecting the environment and improving people’s lives.
通过模仿大自然，科学家已经为保护环境、改善人们的生活提供了许多可能。

20
00:01:49,090 --> 00:01:52,340
As one scientist said, “Nature is our best teacher.
正如一位科学家所说：“大自然是我们最好的老师。

21
00:01:53,140 --> 00:01:57,850
This invention shows people’s creativity and the value of learning from nature.”
这项发明展现了人们的创造力以及向大自然学习的价值。”
